= Three-quadratic support and composite graph edges
24 November2026 · Rust source qualification · Producer evidence UNVERIFIED

Opt-in production modules now check three-small/three-quadratic principal support, subtract a checked one-LP anchor with both original function witnesses retained, and feed composite incidence into the existing signed deferred graph. Twenty-six native controls and strict worker/test Clippy pass. No saved public-curve finder experiment yet. [pcc:unverified]

#image("graph.svg",width:100%)

== Exact boundary
The materializer rechecks the normalized function and norm, complete factorization, actual small ordinates, all three signed Mumford divisors and denominator units. The graph adapter admits a smooth degree7 curve, odd-prime field and exact ordered/oriented factor base. Principal proofs have no unchecked deserializer. Composite edges keep both original principal proofs and their signed coefficient; they are not serialized as one degree-nine function.

Before final projection, every original function is rechecked and large incidence must cancel over integers. Small coefficients are reduced modulo the caller's subgroup order only afterward. A two-endpoint edge without a known endpoint remains deferred. Self-cancellation is a trivial control and never enters the graph. [pcc:unverified]

== Controls and actual result
A deliberately structured smooth F11 fixture has a seven-small/one-quadratic anchor. Fixed lexicographic enumeration reaches its first three-small/three-quadratic function after307 points,59 quartic requests,58 split refusals and0 support refusals. Norm/support/group and composite incidence replay. The resulting edge remains deferred; it produces no ungrounded full relation. These are fixture-generation counts, not measured public-curve yield. [pcc:unverified]

Norm, sign, incidence, factor-base orientation and singular-curve tampering are refused. Existing constructor/support, bounded splitter and signed/deferred graph controls pass. The native source harness reports26 tests,0 failures. Exact source, binary and dependency hashes plus initial/final logs are retained in source-worker-inputs.sha256 and validation/. Scoped optimized compilation uses pinned Root41 libraries; whole-root compilation remains separate. [pcc:unverified]

PCC-20261124-c193f2 is unsigned and UNVERIFIED. Counter coverage is partial. No public-curve relation count, graph-rank gain, full native total, timing rank or parity conclusion. [pcc:unverified]

